{'symbol': 'FE', 'date': '2021-11-15 16:40:00', 'title': 'FIRSTENERGY ENCOURAGES CUSTOMERS TO SHOP FOR BEST ENERGY DEALS AS FUEL COSTS RISE', 'text': 'AKRON, OHIO, NOV. 15, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0WITH HIGHER FUEL COSTS EXPECTED TO INFLUENCE ENERGY RATES THIS WINTER, FIRSTENERGY CORP. (NYSE: FE) IS ENCOURAGING CUSTOMERS OF ITS UTILITY COMPANIES IN OHIO, PENNSYLVANIA, NEW JERSEY AND MARYLAND TO EVALUATE ELECTRIC SUPPLY DEALS THAT FIT THEIR BUDGET AND PROTECT AGAINST RISING ENERGY PRICES. THE PRICE OF NATURAL GAS – WHICH MAKES UP THE LARGEST SHARE OF U.S. ELECTRICITY GENERATION – HAS BEEN RISING IN RECENT MONTHS DUE TO LOW INVENTORY LEVELS AND CONTINUING DEMAND.'}{'symbol': 'FE', 'date': '2021-11-15 15:35:00', 'title': 'MET-ED CONDUCTS ANNUAL STORM RESTORATION DRILL TO HELP EMPLOYEES PREPARE FOR REAL-LIFE EVENTS', 'text': 'READING, PA., NOV. 15, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0MET-ED, A SUBSIDIARY OF FIRSTENERGY CORP. (NYSE: FE), RECENTLY COMPLETED ITS YEARLY EMERGENCY PREPARATION DRILL FOCUSED ON TESTING ITS STORM RESTORATION PROCESS IN THE EVENT SEVERE WEATHER CAUSES WIDESPREAD OUTAGES THROUGHOUT ITS SERVICE AREA.'}